--Strategy:
-- 1) Filter SAMPLE_CONTENTS to rows where sample_path ends with composer.json (case‑insensitive).
-- 2) Parse the “content” column as JSON and access its "require" object.
-- 3) Use LATERAL FLATTEN to turn each key/value pair inside "require" into its own row.
-- 4) Select rows whose package name contains the substring 'laravel' (ILIKE '%laravel%').
--This keeps JSON parsing (so we truly look at the require section) while broadening the match.
--Finally, LIMIT 20 for a quick preview.
